# SER.SCR - INVTEST on VM B's COM1 against INVSERV's serial port (run by
# srvgate.sh after NET2.SCR): the line names its station in HELLO, the
# session list shows its kind, and a page of over 2 KB travels between
# two PINGs in flight with it.  After BYE the port listens again, for
# the INV /CMD /COM1 run that follows.

@COM 1 COM1
> HELLO RISER
< +OK
> LOGIN ADMIN Srv2gate
< +OK LEVEL=3 NAME="System Administrator"
> ADMIN CLIENTS
< +DATA
< F SLOT TYPE STATION USER LEVEL STATE IDLE SELF
<* R * COM1 RISER ADMIN 3 3 * 1
< .
>& PING
>& ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID,MFR,DESCR,TAGS PAGE=25
>& PING
@WAIT 1
< +OK
@WAIT 1
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID MFR DESCR TAGS
@WAIT 1
< +OK
> BYE
< +OK
